The file src/data/lmsdCurated.json is a derived index (curated sum-composition
membership per lipid class) built from an LMSD structures.sdf release via
scripts/ingest-lmsd.ts. It contains counts and classification, not full structures.

LIPID MAPS Structure Database (LMSD):
  Sud M, Fahy E, Cotter D, et al. LMSD: LIPID MAPS structure database.
  Nucleic Acids Res. 2007;35(Database):D527-D532. doi:10.1093/nar/gkl838

This product includes ml/sascorer.py and ml/fpscores.pkl.gz, vendored unmodified
from the RDKit project's Contrib/SA_Score (BSD 3-Clause License).
Source: https://github.com/rdkit/rdkit/tree/master/Contrib/SA_Score

Synthetic accessibility score:
  Ertl P, Schuffenhauer A. Estimation of synthetic accessibility score of
  drug-like molecules based on molecular complexity and fragment contributions.
  J Cheminform. 2009;1:8. doi:10.1186/1758-2946-1-8

This product includes ml/data/raw/pnnl_ccs_compendium.tsv, the "Unified CCS Compendium"
from Pacific Northwest National Laboratory (Baker lab), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. Source: https://github.com/PNNL-Comp-Mass-Spec/MetabolomicsCCS
Used as real, drift-tube-measured collision cross section data to calibrate and
validate the CCS property model (ml/data_prep.py, ml/train.py) — not modified beyond
filtering/reshaping into ml/data/processed/real_lipid_ccs.csv.

The file src/data/phaseDiagrams/dopcDppcChol.json contains tie-line coordinates for the
DOPC/DPPC/cholesterol ternary phase diagram, hand-transcribed from Table A.1 of:
  Marsh D. Cholesterol-induced fluid membrane domains: A compendium of lipid-raft
  ternary phase diagrams. Biochim Biophys Acta 1788 (2009) 2114-2123.
  doi:10.1016/j.bbamem.2009.08.004
which itself re-tabulates data originally measured by:
  Veatch SL, Gawrisch K, Keller SL. Closed-loop miscibility gap and quantitative
  tie-lines in ternary membrane mixtures. Biophys J 90 (2006) 4428-4436.
Unlike the LMSD (CC BY 4.0) and PNNL (Apache 2.0) sources above, these two papers
are standard-copyright journal articles, not openly licensed for redistribution.
Only the numerical tie-line coordinates (facts, not the papers' text or figures) are
reproduced here, transcribed by hand for use in src/lib/phaseDiagram.ts.
